The research concludes that cloud storage buckets are essential resources in modern computing environments but remain highly susceptible to security incidents when misconfigured. Current research between 2024 and 2026 consistently identifies storage exposure, weak IAM implementation, inadequate monitoring, and poor governance practices as major contributors to cloud security incidents. (Cloud Security Alliance Releases, CSA 2026)
Effective cloud bucket security requires a combination of least-privilege access, encryption, continuous monitoring, configuration reviews, and automated compliance controls. (docs.aws.amazon.com)

  Recommendations
1.	Enforce least-privilege IAM policies.
2.	Enable encryption for all bucket data.
3.	Block public access by default.
4.	Enable audit logging and continuous monitoring.
5.	Regularly review bucket permissions.
6.	Implement versioning and backup strategies.
7.	Deploy Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM) tools.
8.	Conduct periodic security audits and compliance reviews.
9.	Automate configuration assessment using policy-as-code.
10.	Train cloud administrators on secure configuration practices. (docs.aws.amazon.com)
